1. Root Node

The root is a special empty node.

TrieNode root = new TrieNode();

It does not represent any character.

          root

The root's job is to hold references to the first characters of all words.

If we insert:

cat
car
dog

Root will have:

          root
         /    \
        c      d

So yes:

Root keeps references to its children.

2. Trie Node Structure

Most common implementation:

class TrieNode {

    TrieNode[] children = new TrieNode[26];

    boolean isEndOfWord;
}

Each node stores:

children[0] -> a
children[1] -> b
children[2] -> c
...
children[25] -> z

and

isEndOfWord

which tells us whether a complete word ends here.

